<title>JAPAN: TOKYO STOCKS END LOWER ON RENEWED BANKING FEARS.</title>
<headline>TOKYO STOCKS END LOWER ON RENEWED BANKING FEARS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese stocks met with a renewed wave of sales on Monday, with the key market index closing two percent lower.</p>
<p>Brokers said overall sentiment was dampened by reignited fears over the banking sectors' profitability.</p>
</text>
